 # Changelog
 
+## 0.4.2 (unreleased)
+
+Ignore-aware repository walk (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#417, for Pulse blueprint/watch/ledger). Additive: no existing item changed. std only, every platform, independent of the index.
+
+- `walk_repo(root, &WalkOptions, visitor) -> io::Result<WalkOutcome>`: depth-first, file-name-ordered traversal that skips what `.gitignore` excludes. Honours nested `.gitignore` files (deeper overrides shallower, last matching rule wins), negation (`!`), directory-only rules (`dir/`), anchoring, `*`, `?`, `[a-z]`, `\` escapes and `**` (leading, middle, trailing), plus `.git/info/exclude`. `.git` is never reported or entered; ignored directories are not entered, so nothing below them is re-included (git's rule).
+- `WalkOptions` (`#[non_exhaustive]`, build from `Default`): `ignore_file_names` (default `.gitignore`; add `.ignore`), `use_git_info_exclude`, `extra_ignore_files` (e.g. the global excludes file, lowest precedence), `skip_hidden`, `max_depth`, `max_entries`, `case_insensitive` (default on Windows and macOS).
+- Visitor returns `WalkControl::{Continue, SkipDir, Stop}`; `WalkEntry { path, rel_path (always '/'), depth, kind: WalkKind, size }`; `WalkOutcome { entries, ignored, errors, truncated }`. An unreadable subdirectory is counted, not fatal. Symlinks are reported as `WalkKind::Symlink` and never followed.
+- `GitIgnore` (`new`, `push_rules(base, text)`, `pop_rules`, `is_ignored(rel_path, is_dir)`) is public for callers that run their own traversal.
+- Not covered: reading `core.excludesFile` from git config (pass the file through `extra_ignore_files`) and `.gitattributes`.
+
 ## 0.4.1 (2026-10-17)
 
 - Depend on rightkit-child-process 0.5.0 (and rightkit-sandbox 0.5.0 where used); no behaviour change.
